# LaTeX build artifacts and scratch renders (regenerate with: python build.py)
build/
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# No assembled volume and no PDF is ever published. Only the Markdown chapters
# and the projects are. These are blanket rules rather than named files, so a new
# output name cannot slip through: the whole volume, a single chapter, or
# anything else.
*.pdf
*.html

# Named explicitly as well, so the intent survives anyone relaxing the rules above.
rtos-embedded-linux.pdf
rtos-embedded-linux.html
chapter-*.pdf
chapter-*.html

# --- The authoring half, which is not published ---------------------------
#
# What this repository publishes is Markdown: one chapter under chapters/, one
# project under projects/, and each chapter's figures with the project they
# belong to. The LaTeX those are generated FROM stays on the authoring machine.
# A reader needs neither a TeX installation nor a second copy of every chapter in
# a second markup language to read the book.
#
# The loop is: edit sections/zNN.tex, then
#     python mdbuild.py --out build/md
#     python scripts/publish.py
# and publish.py writes chapters/ and the per-project figure directories.
# Nothing else writes chapters/.
#
# No LaTeX of any kind is published, figure sources included. One blanket rule
# rather than a list of paths, because a list is something a new file can be
# added outside of: this cannot be got round by putting a .tex somewhere new.
#
# The anchored rules below are still here on purpose. *.tex already covers the
# .tex among them, but sections/ and figures/ are directories whose other
# contents must also stay out, and naming the scripts keeps the authoring half
# readable as a set rather than as a side effect of a glob.
*.tex

# Every rule here is anchored with a leading slash so it matches only at the
# repository root. Without the anchor, "figures/" would also ignore all twenty
# projects/NN-slug/docs/figures/ directories, where the published SVGs live.
/sections/
/figures/
/build.py
/mdbuild.py
/crosscheck.py
/lint.py
/figcheck.sh

# Cargo's build output. One directory at the workspace root, which is where cargo
# puts it. Cargo.lock is NOT ignored for the edition crates: three crates building
# one source should resolve to one dependency set, and a lock file is how that is
# checked rather than hoped.
projects/01-presence/rust/target/
projects/02-the-claim/rust/target/

# Local virtual environments and editor state
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Journals and correspondence never reach a published repository, private shares
# included. They live in the catalogue, which is local only. A published
# repository carries the work, never the running record of doing it.
private_journal/
correspondence/
DIARY*.md

# A kernel cloned for the FreeRTOS adapter is not this repository's code. The
# Makefile puts it outside the tree by default; this is here so that a clone made
# inside one by hand cannot be committed by accident.
third_party/
FreeRTOS-Kernel/
